[{"id":29985,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/29985\">#1</a> I just finished writing a comment in the measuring coalgebra thread, and was informed on the first go that my comment was 131 characters too long, so I cut it a little short. I’ve never seen that before; has anyone else? What is the character limit?</p>","timestamp":1332063991,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":29992,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/29992\">#2</a> How many characters long did your comment end up being?</p>\n<p>(I’ve moved this discussion to the n-Forum category.)</p>","timestamp":1332091395,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":29993,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/29993\">#3</a> Is there an easy way to find out?</p>","timestamp":1332092011,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":29995,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/29995\">#4</a> I assume that it’s <a href=\"#narrow/channel/15/topic/discussion.20on.20measuring.20coalgebras/near/29984\">this comment</a>.  So I copied the source to a text file and ran the Unix utility (actually GNU utility now) <code>wc</code> on it: it has 5711 characters (all of which are ASCII).  So the limit is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5711</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5711 + n - 33</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5711</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">33</span></span></span></span>, where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n \\geq 33</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">33</span></span></span></span> is the number of characters that you removed after the error message.</p>","timestamp":1332093353,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":29999,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/29999\">#5</a> The maximum comment length is currently set to 6000 characters.  I’m quite happy to raise it further.  There will always be <em>some</em> limit, though.</p>","timestamp":1332099880,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":30001,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/comment.20too.20long/near/30001\">#6</a> Thanks, Andrew – I expect it’s probably not necessary: that comment was a bit of an outlier. It merely took me by surprise.</p>","timestamp":1332102523,"subject":"comment too long","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]